  {
    "submission": "submission_c27.json",
    "summary": "Second scenario check (action=check) for the already-accepted requirement unit-claim-timeout-now-attribution, measuring the consequence the finding's importance rests on; preflight-validated with valid=True and no diagnostics. Kept with the same obligation rather than split into a new question.\n\nDesign: plan_c5.json plus harness_tnvote_test.go build voter nodes with background goroutines disabled, each with a bootstrapped three-voter configuration and a known leader (node2), and drive RequestVote through the production dispatch processRPC in three cases: the privileged case (configured candidate node3, LeadershipTransfer true) and two controls (the identical request without the flag, and the flag with a candidate absent from the configuration). Declarative prerequisite: transfer_privilege_set true, candidate_is_configured_voter true, receiver_has_leader true. Monitor applicability: the privilege set and a configured candidate. Property: the voter grants the vote in the privileged case, identity op_id, evaluated from emitted event fields rather than tests_passed.\n\nConstruction evidence (not the formal observation): a local run in a copy of the captured module produced exactly the pattern the scenario is about — granted true with the flag, granted false without it, and granted false when the candidate is not in the configuration — so the privilege really does override leader stickiness while leaving the membership check intact.\n\nDeclared limits: the scenario assumes the flag is set (whether an unattributed sender can cause it to be set is the claim's separate open premise), there is no live cluster or timing, and only the grant decision is measured, not the resulting election. No target code was modified; the nodes use skipStartup and the known leader is set through the same accessors appendEntries uses.\n\nRun state: four confirmed in-scope violations, no pending review work; this product adds measurement of a confirmed finding's mechanism rather than a new question."
